A||N||35||CozmoPooky||"Stealth" Fiero ?||||5||
Z||000000||CozmoPooky||12-12-2000||07:52 AM||||St. Pete is starting to use "courtesy" radar signs that measure and show a car's speed on a large roadside display (to discourage speeding, I guess).  Driving by one this A.M. I noticed that the car in front of me triggered it much further away than I did in my Fiero. I turned around and tried it a couple more times and it seems that the Fiero's "detection distance" was about half that of most other vehicles.<BR>   I don't know much about stealth technology, but does the non-metallic body and lack of forward reflecting surfaces make the Fiero harder to "see" on radar?  (BTW, Florida doesn't have front plates, which I understand to be excellent reflectors for both radar and laser devices).<BR>   Is there any truth in this, or do I need to check my Meds? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">?  <P>------------------<BR>CozmoPooky<BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>'87 Duke Coupe<BR>'85 2M6 Targa||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-12-2000||08:46 AM||||The soft plastic features of the Fiero especially the GT nose do not reflect the radar back at the same rate as the metallic monsters on the road. There are very few "flat" spots on the front of the car to get a fix. The car is also a lot lower than other cars, so aiming the radar gun may also be an infuence.  So in some instances the Fiero is invisable to the radar at a greater distance.  But as you saw by your experiment, it does see you.  And a small two seater sport car makes a good target for a traffic stop just by going down the road at a high rate of speed.||||reg||3
Z||000002||afRaceR||12-12-2000||12:14 PM||||I noticed the same thing this weekend. I was driving to my parents house and on the way I went through a he!! of a lot of construction and I went through two of those things. I noticed that both times it took longer to read my speed and it was slower than I was going. <P>These were two completely different units. The first one was 5 miles slower and the second was 6 miles slower. I don't know if it was skipping over me and going for the cars behind me though. I think I will change my mind about putting that front license plate frame on my 85 GT for awhile.<BR>Especially since I will be driving to Montgomery the first of January.||||reg||1
