Z||000015||Oreif||12-12-2000||09:00 PM||||Yes there is a way to burn-out the receiving detector on a police radar. It isn't that complicated at all. You just need the freq they are using (10.4 GHz or 24.4Ghz) a specific pulse rate (497.5mhz) and a directional antenna (or 2 antenna's). The problem comes into play in the power required. In order to fry them out you need 4 times the power the receiving detector is looking for. With those power requirements, you are looking at a very expensive amplifier. Not to mention putting out that much power would also be a very large beacon if they wanted to find you. The trucker probably only turned it on when needed and since we heard about it he was caught.<BR>Besides it's easier to "stealth" past then to actively jam them. (also it is legal to absorb radar emissions where it is illegal to transmit at those freq's.) So spend lots of money to build a jamming unit that could land you in jail with large fines or add about 100 pounds to the car and absorb the radar waves so the radar can't see you.<BR>Of course that would be the day they are using the laser unit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
